# /Users/nickyrice/Documents/seymour-guide/seymour/.gitignore

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — the category that can cost you real money.
# .env holds API keys and credentials. Committing one publishes it.
# See §6.7 for what actually happens. Note we allow .env.example
# (with fake values) so the file's SHAPE is documented in the repo.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MODEL WEIGHTS — tens of gigabytes. Git stores EVERY version forever,
# so one 35 GB file committed twice is 70 GB of history that every
# clone must download. GitHub rejects files over 100 MB anyway.
# Weights are downloaded, not authored: they belong in a cache, and
# the code that fetches them belongs in the repo instead.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.mlx

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PYTHON — .venv is thousands of files that can be rebuilt in seconds
# from your dependency list. __pycache__ is compiled bytecode: machine-
# specific, regenerated automatically, pure noise in a diff.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NODE — same logic. node_modules/ can exceed 100k files and is fully
# reconstructible from package-lock.json.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
out/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL STATE — databases, logs, and anything else this machine
# generates. Not source. Not shareable. Often contains your data.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.db
*.sqlite3
logs/
*.log

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS — .DS_Store is a Finder metadata file that appears in every
# directory you open. Harmless, useless, and it will otherwise show up
# in every diff you ever make.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
# Local model weights folder (capitalized on this machine) and build metadata.
Models/
*.egg-info/
